# `Promise` and `console` are globals that a program may replace, and so is `console.log`. No body of this program writes them, so Link takes each for what the table says lies there, and the program locks each when it starts
# The object that console.log is passed is only looked at, and the function that the construction is passed is entered by the row alone
# new Promise(run); console.log({ x: "s" });
